  "answer_core": "I would not lock in 15% equity, a board seat, and a CTO title this week. Those are long‑term commitments you can only make after seeing whether the partnership actually strengthens the company rather than concentrating risk in one person.\n\nFriday should be a direct, structured conversation about a staged path. Make clear that you’re open to major upside for him, but only after evidence. Set a short, defined period to test: whether he can deliver the key platform work, whether that work matters for revenue, whether team continuity improves rather than worsens, whether knowledge transfer happens, and whether his behavior fits the governance you need. Spell out what success in that window would unlock.\n\nKeep the discussion on proof and company health, not on hypothetical valuations. The goal is to avoid both a premature commitment and a vague delay that pushes him away. Give him a real path forward, but one tied to demonstrated impact.",
